{"name":"Bull Kelp","hex":"#636153","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"bull kelp","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The brown alga Nereocystis luetkeana."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bull_kelp"}],"entries":[{"title":"Bull kelp","blocks":[{"text":"Bull kelp is a common name for the brown alga Nereocystis luetkeana which is a true kelp in the family Laminariaceae. It grows in coastal waters. It ranges from Unimak Island, Alaska to California, but there is more of it north of San Francisco."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bull_kelp"},{"title":"Bull","blocks":[{"text":"A bull is an intact adult male of the species Bos taurus (cattle). More muscular and aggressive than the females of the same species, bulls have long been an important symbol in many religions, including for sacrifices. These animals play a significant role in beef ranching, dairy farming, and a variety of sporting and cultural activities, including bullfighting and bull riding."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b5/A_Friesian_Bull%2C_Llandeilo_Graban_-_geograph.org.uk_-_579885.jpg/330px-A_Friesian_Bull%2C_Llandeilo_Graban_-_geograph.org.uk_-_579885.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bull"},{"title":"Kelp","blocks":[{"text":"Kelps are large brown algae or seaweeds that make up the order Laminariales. There are about 30 genera. Despite its appearance and use of photosynthesis in chloroplasts, kelp is not a plant but a stramenopile."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/28/Kelp_In_Freycinet_Tasmania.jpg/330px-Kelp_In_Freycinet_Tasmania.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kelp"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/59/Nereocystis_luetkeana1.jpg/250px-Nereocystis_luetkeana1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.or